    },
    {
      "id": "plan-detail", "type": "view", "label": "Topological adjacency detail", "root": false,
      "position": {"x": -280, "y": -520}, "width": 500, "height": 260,
      "ports": [{"id": "root", "key": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "input", "dataType": "any", "angle": 180}],
      "handles": [{"id": "root", "portId": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "input", "dataType": "any", "angle": 180}],
      "visible": true, "showLabel": true,
      "data": {"view": {"payload": "node.web.detail"}, "html": "<article style='height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;padding:24px;border-radius:22px;background:#111827;color:#f8fafc;font-family:system-ui'><div style='font:800 11px/1 system-ui;color:#67e8f9'>WORKSPACE TOPOLOGY</div><h2 style='margin:14px 0 10px;font-size:30px'>Bridges define adjacency, not position.</h2><p style='margin:0;color:#cbd5e1;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55'>Move a graph anywhere. Its authored bridges remain intact. Workspace regions and apertures adapt around the new embedding.</p></article>"}
    },
    {
      "id": "plan-summary", "type": "view", "label": "Topological adjacency summary", "root": false,
      "position": {"x": 280, "y": -520}, "width": 380, "height": 210,
      "ports": [{"id": "root", "key": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "input", "dataType": "any", "angle": 180}],
      "handles": [{"id": "root", "portId": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "input", "dataType": "any", "angle": 180}],
      "visible": true, "showLabel": true,
      "data": {"view": {"payload": "node.web.summary"}, "html": "<div style='height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;padding:20px;border-radius:18px;background:#111827;color:#f8fafc;font-family:system-ui'><strong style='font-size:22px'>Topology first.</strong><p style='color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.5'>Semantic bridges stay fixed while workspace regions, shared boundaries, and apertures are derived from the current embedding.</p></div>"}
    },
    {
      "id": "plan-icon", "type": "view", "label": "Topology icon", "root": false,
      "position": {"x": 720, "y": -520}, "width": 190, "height": 140,
      "ports": [{"id": "root", "key": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "input", "dataType": "any", "angle": 180}],
      "handles": [{"id": "root", "portId": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "input", "dataType": "any", "angle": 180}],
      "visible": true, "showLabel": true,
      "data": {"view": {"payload": "node.web.icon"}, "html": "<div style='height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;padding:18px;border-radius:18px;background:#111827;color:#f8fafc;font-family:system-ui'><div style='font-size:30px'>⬡</div><div style='margin-top:12px;font-weight:800'>Adjacency regions</div></div>"}
    },
    {
      "id": "plan-glyph", "type": "glyph", "label": "Topology", "root": false,
      "position": {"x": 960, "y": -500}, "width": 90, "height": 90,
      "ports": [{"id": "root", "key": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "input", "dataType": "any", "angle": 180}],
      "handles": [{"id": "root", "portId": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "input", "dataType": "any", "angle": 180}],
      "visible": true, "showLabel": true,
      "data": {"view": {"payload": "node.web.glyph"}, "glyph": "⬡"}
    },
    {
      "id": "plan-root", "type": "content", "label": "Workspace Topological Adjacency", "root": true,
      "position": {"x": -800, "y": 0}, "width": 520, "height": 330,
      "ports": [{"id": "root", "key": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "bidirectional", "dataType": "any", "angle": 180}, {"id": "next", "key": "next", "label": "goal", "direction": "output", "dataType": "navigation", "angle": 0}],
      "handles": [{"id": "root", "portId": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "bidirectional", "dataType": "any", "angle": 180}, {"id": "next", "portId": "next", "label": "goal", "direction": "output", "dataType": "navigation", "angle": 0}],
      "visible": true, "showLabel": true,
      "data": {"content": {"kind": "markdown", "value": "# Workspace Topological Adjacency\n\n## Core invariant\n\n**Bridges dictate adjacency. Graph position does not.**\n\nMoving a graph changes only the workspace embedding. The authored bridge topology remains fixed, while graph regions, shared boundaries, and apertures are recomputed around the new arrangement."}}
    },
    {
      "id": "goal-topology", "type": "content", "label": "Goal · topology survives movement", "root": false,
      "position": {"x": -130, "y": 0}, "width": 500, "height": 270,
      "ports": [{"id": "root", "key": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "input", "dataType": "navigation", "angle": 180}, {"id": "next", "key": "next", "label": "architecture", "direction": "output", "dataType": "navigation", "angle": 0}],
      "handles": [{"id": "root", "portId": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "input", "dataType": "navigation", "angle": 180}, {"id": "next", "portId": "next", "label": "architecture", "direction": "output", "dataType": "navigation", "angle": 0}],
      "visible": true, "showLabel": true,
      "data": {"content": {"kind": "markdown", "value": "# Goal: topology survives movement\n\nDragging or resizing a graph changes the **workspace embedding**, not the authored topology.\n\nBridge adjacency remains authoritative. Graph-local node coordinates remain graph-local. Workspace geometry never dirties graph documents."}}
    },
    {
      "id": "decision-three-layers", "type": "content", "label": "Decision · separate three layers", "root": false,
      "position": {"x": 520, "y": 0}, "width": 540, "height": 330,
      "ports": [{"id": "root", "key": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "input", "dataType": "navigation", "angle": 180}, {"id": "next", "key": "next", "label": "implementation", "direction": "output", "dataType": "navigation", "angle": 0}],
      "handles": [{"id": "root", "portId": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "input", "dataType": "navigation", "angle": 180}, {"id": "next", "portId": "next", "label": "implementation", "direction": "output", "dataType": "navigation", "angle": 0}],
      "visible": true, "showLabel": true,
      "data": {"content": {"kind": "markdown", "value": "# Decision: three layers\n\n1. **Semantic topology**: authored bridge says Graph A is adjacent to Graph B.\n2. **Workspace topology**: derive which graph regions share boundaries and apertures.\n3. **Geometry**: derive the actual paths, shapes, hit regions, and minimap projection for the current embedding.\n\nPresentation must not rewrite structure."}}
    },
    {
      "id": "task-audit", "type": "content", "label": "Task · audit current geometry", "root": false,
      "position": {"x": 1230, "y": -300}, "width": 460, "height": 250,
      "ports": [{"id": "root", "key": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "input", "dataType": "navigation", "angle": 180}],
      "handles": [{"id": "root", "portId": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "input", "dataType": "navigation", "angle": 180}],
      "visible": true, "showLabel": true,
      "data": {"content": {"kind": "markdown", "value": "# Audit current frame geometry\n\nTrace rectangular frame bounds, drag state, resize state, hit testing, focus, and minimap calculations. Identify every place that assumes a graph workspace region must be rectangular."}}
    },
    {
      "id": "task-region", "type": "content", "label": "Task · define region model", "root": false,
      "position": {"x": 1230, "y": 20}, "width": 460, "height": 270,
      "ports": [{"id": "root", "key": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "input", "dataType": "navigation", "angle": 180}],
      "handles": [{"id": "root", "portId": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "input", "dataType": "navigation", "angle": 180}],
      "visible": true, "showLabel": true,
      "data": {"content": {"kind": "markdown", "value": "# Define a derived workspace region model\n\nA graph owns a workspace region around its content extent. The region may be non-rectangular and must expose shared-boundary information without changing graph-local content coordinates."}}
    },
    {
      "id": "task-resolver", "type": "content", "label": "Task · adjacency resolver", "root": false,
      "position": {"x": 1780, "y": -300}, "width": 460, "height": 270,
      "ports": [{"id": "root", "key": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "input", "dataType": "navigation", "angle": 180}],
      "handles": [{"id": "root", "portId": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "input", "dataType": "navigation", "angle": 180}],
      "visible": true, "showLabel": true,
      "data": {"content": {"kind": "markdown", "value": "# Build the adjacency resolver\n\nConsume only authored bridge relationships. Produce workspace-only adjacency constraints for open graphs. Graph position influences the embedding but never deletes or rewrites bridge adjacency."}}
    },
    {
      "id": "task-boundaries", "type": "content", "label": "Task · shared boundaries", "root": false,
      "position": {"x": 1780, "y": 20}, "width": 460, "height": 280,
      "ports": [{"id": "root", "key": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "input", "dataType": "navigation", "angle": 180}],
      "handles": [{"id": "root", "portId": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "input", "dataType": "navigation", "angle": 180}],
      "visible": true, "showLabel": true,
      "data": {"content": {"kind": "markdown", "value": "# Derive shared boundaries and apertures\n\nWhen bridged graph regions are adjacent, derive a common boundary and place the aperture on it. The current corridor rails disappear once shared-boundary geometry becomes authoritative."}}
    },
    {
      "id": "task-reembed", "type": "content", "label": "Task · re-embed on movement", "root": false,
      "position": {"x": 2330, "y": -300}, "width": 460, "height": 270,
      "ports": [{"id": "root", "key": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "input", "dataType": "navigation", "angle": 180}],
      "handles": [{"id": "root", "portId": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "input", "dataType": "navigation", "angle": 180}],
      "visible": true, "showLabel": true,
      "data": {"content": {"kind": "markdown", "value": "# Re-embed on graph movement\n\nDragging a graph updates the current 2D embedding and recomputes regions while preserving bridge topology, graph-local coordinates, and clean document state."}}
    },
    {
      "id": "task-minimap", "type": "content", "label": "Task · minimap projection", "root": false,
      "position": {"x": 2330, "y": 20}, "width": 460, "height": 260,
      "ports": [{"id": "root", "key": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "input", "dataType": "navigation", "angle": 180}],
      "handles": [{"id": "root", "portId": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "input", "dataType": "navigation", "angle": 180}],
      "visible": true, "showLabel": true,
      "data": {"content": {"kind": "markdown", "value": "# Project the same model into the minimap\n\nWorkspace-scope minimap rendering must consume the same derived regions and apertures. Do not create a second adjacency geometry system."}}
    },
    {
      "id": "questions", "type": "content", "label": "Open questions", "root": false,
      "position": {"x": 2890, "y": -120}, "width": 560, "height": 430,
      "ports": [{"id": "root", "key": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "input", "dataType": "navigation", "angle": 180}],
      "handles": [{"id": "root", "portId": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "input", "dataType": "navigation", "angle": 180}],
      "visible": true, "showLabel": true,
      "data": {"content": {"kind": "markdown", "value": "# Open questions\n\n- **Region algorithm:** What is the simplest stable shape model? Orthogonal polygons, padded hulls, Voronoi-like regions, or a staged approach?\n- **Conflicting adjacency:** How should the workspace embed several bridge constraints that cannot all be represented as simple pairwise boundaries?\n- **Resize semantics:** If borders are derived, does resize mean a preferred workspace envelope rather than a literal frame?\n- **Interaction:** What part of an amorphous region owns drag, focus, selection, and resize affordances?"}}
    }
  ],
